    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d245">

                <pb facs="0476" n="372" sameAs="frus:frus1933v02/pg372"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">548.D1/40: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to the Consul at Geneva
                        (Gilbert)</hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Washington</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1933-10-24T16:00:00-05:00">October 24, 1933—4
                            p.m.</date>
                    </dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>112. Your 263, October 17, paragraph 3, and your 246, paragraph 1 (<hi
                        rendition="#italic">c</hi>),<anchor n="28" xml:id="d245-f1"/> please
                    indicate informally to Avenol that this Government does not desire to
                    participate in the choice of a High Commissioner.</p>
                <pb facs="0477" n="373" xml:id="pg373"/>
                <p>Your 263, October 17, paragraph 4, you should informally suggest to Avenol, in
                    the event that an endeavor is made to obtain an American as High Commissioner,
                    that this Government would prefer that the matter be handled under alternative
                        C.<anchor n="29" xml:id="d245-f2"/>
                </p>
                <p>For your information, an acceptance of the League’s invitation as set forth in
                    your 259, October 14<anchor n="30" xml:id="d245-f3"/> will be cabled to Bern for
                    delivery.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Hull</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d245-f1" n="28" xml:id="d245-f1-content">
                <p>Neither printed.</p>
            </note>
            <note corresp="#d245-f2" n="29" xml:id="d245-f2-content">
                <p>The three alternatives suggested for obtaining an American High Commissioner
                    were: <quote rend="blockquote">
                        <list>
                            <item>“(A) To ask the American Government if it desires to ‘nominate’ or
                                to ‘suggest’ an individual;</item>
                            <item>“(B) To present the name of an American national to the Government
                                and inquire whether the United States ‘is agreeable to’ or ‘has any
                                objection to’ his appointment;</item>
                            <item>“(C) To offer the appointment direct to an American national,
                                leaving to him entirely the matter of his taking it up with
                                Washington if he so desires.” (548.D1/29)</item>
                        </list>
                    </quote>
                </p>
            </note>
            <note corresp="#d245-f3" n="30" xml:id="d245-f3-content">
                <p>Not printed.</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
    </standOff>
